To make the prereq image:

  qemu-img create -f qcow2 -b w8.qcow2 prereq.qcow2
  kvm -m 1G -net nic -net user,hostfwd=tcp:127.0.0.1:10022-:22 -drive file=prereq.qcow2 -nographic
  # In another window:
  scp -P 10022 -i vagrant-key uf-prereq vagrant@localhost:
  scp -P 10022 -i vagrant-key -r whl vagrant@localhost:
  ssh -p 10022 -i vagrant-key vagrant@localhost sh uf-prereq

The base image came from "Vagrant up" and then the VDMK was
converted to qcow2. Install Cygwin, including the following:
make, wget, rsync, openssh-server
Start a cygwin terminal in Admin mode and then use ssh-host-config
to turn on SSHd as a service. see http://www.noah.org/ssh/cygwin-sshd.html

To edit the base image:

  kvm -m 700M -net nic -net user,hostfwd=tcp:127.0.0.1:10022-:22 -drive file=w8.qcow2

(user Vagrant, pass: vagrant)

